# Culvert Maintenance Agent — sudoers allowlist
#
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for which `docker compose`
# invocations the agent is allowed to run when privilege_mode=sudoers
# (the production default; see roadmap/D1.6-maintenance-agent-
# implementation-plan.md § 4.5).
#
# The agent's command runner prepends `sudo -n` to every templated
# invocation; sudo's exact-arg matching enforces that the agent cannot
# deviate from this list, even with an in-process bug.
#
# Adding a new operation requires the four-step contract from § 4.6:
#   1. Typed API handler in the agent.
#   2. Command template in internal/runner.
#   3. Sudoers allowlist entry HERE (this file).
#   4. Tests, including the parity test that asserts every runner
#      template has a matching line and vice versa.
#
# Skipping any of the four is a review block.
#
# D1.6a scope: only the minimal `docker compose ps` entry needed by
# /v1/status. NO backup, restore, cleanup, upgrade, rollback, up, down,
# pull, or manifest-inspect entries in this file. Those land with their
# corresponding operations:
#   - D1.6b adds run --rm cli --backup, --restore, --restore --confirm,
#     --cleanup-restore-leftovers, up -d, down.
#   - D1.6c adds pull proxy and manifest inspect <allowed-image>.
#
# Operator install steps:
#   1. Replace {compose_project_dir} below with the absolute path to
#      your compose project (the dir containing docker-compose.yml).
#   2. Replace {compose_file} with the actual filename (typically
#      docker-compose.yml).
#   3. Validate the file:    visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/culvert-maint
#   4. Install with mode 0440:
#        install -m 0440 -o root -g root \
#            packaging/sudoers/culvert-maint \
#            /etc/sudoers.d/culvert-maint

# D1.6a — minimal read-only entry for /v1/status.
# Template: compose.status (BaseArgv = ["docker", "compose", "-f",
# "{compose_file}", "ps"])
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_file} ps
